<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <fullName>Provider_Name__c</fullName>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <description>The utility company that bills this meter. Text rather than a lookup to Account, matching the shipped Property Management precedent Work_Order__c.Vendor__c. See the comment below and the open question raised with this build.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>The utility company name exactly as it appears on the invoice, for example CenterPoint Energy. Keep the spelling consistent across meters so that reporting groups them together.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Provider</label>
    <length>120</length>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Text</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
    <!--
      FSD 5.10.4 specifies Lookup(Account) for Provider. Text is recommended instead and the
      deviation is flagged, not taken silently:

      1. Precedent. The only comparable field already shipped in Property Management is
         Work_Order__c.Vendor__c, which is Text(120).
      2. There is no utility provider Account population, and no Account record type for
         vendors; the only two are Broker_Firm and Investor_Entity.
      3. Every criteria sharing rule on Account is keyed on RecordTypeId equals Broker Firm
         or Investor Entity. A provider Account matching neither would fall through all of
         them and be visible only through ownership or OWD, which is the same class of
         defect this build rejected standard Asset over.

      Deliberately named Provider_Name__c and not Provider__c. ARCHITECTURE section 1 asks
      for a _Name__c suffix on Text carrying a human label, and this leaves the API name
      Provider__c free for a future Lookup(Account), so the migration is additive: add the
      lookup, backfill from this field, repoint, retire. Never a rename.
    -->
</CustomField>
